### Configure custom ignored build step

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/monorepos/turborepo

Use this command in the Ignored Build Step project setting to conditionally skip builds based on changes.

```bash
turbo query affected --base=$VERCEL_GIT_PREVIOUS_SHA --packages <your-project-name> --exit-code
```

--------------------------------

### Get Previous Successful Deployment SHA

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/environment-variables/system-environment-variables

Only exposed when an Ignored Build Step is provided. Available at build time.

```bash
REDACTED
```

--------------------------------

### Disable all automatic Git deployments in Vercel

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/project-configuration/git-configuration

Set deploymentEnabled to false to prevent any branch from triggering a deployment.

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://openapi.vercel.sh/vercel.json",
  "git": {
    "deploymentEnabled": false
  }
}
```

```typescript
import type { VercelConfig } from '@vercel/config/v1';

export const config: VercelConfig = {
  git: {
    deploymentEnabled: false,
  },
};
```

--------------------------------

### Configure ignoreCommand in vercel.json

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/project-configuration/vercel-json

Use this to override the default ignored build step behavior. The build continues if the command exits with code 1, and is ignored if it exits with 0.

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://openapi.vercel.sh/vercel.json",
  "ignoreCommand": "git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD ./"
}
```

--------------------------------

### Identify Git Commit Reference

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/environment-variables/framework-environment-variables

Specifies the git branch of the commit that triggered the deployment. Available at both build and runtime.

```bash
REDACTED
```

--------------------------------

### Match multiple branches using minimatch in Vercel

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/project-configuration/git-configuration

Apply deployment rules to groups of branches using glob patterns. This example prevents deployments for any branch starting with internal-.

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://openapi.vercel.sh/vercel.json",
  "git": {
    "deploymentEnabled": {
      "internal-*": false
    }
  }
}
```

```typescript
import type { VercelConfig } from '@vercel/config/v1';

export const config: VercelConfig = {
  git: {
    deploymentEnabled: {
      'internal-*': false,
    },
  },
};
```

--------------------------------

### Define VERCEL_GIT_PREVIOUS_SHA

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/git/vercel-for-bitbucket

Contains the SHA of the last successful deployment; only available when an Ignored Build Step is configured.

```bash
REDACTED
```

--------------------------------

### Next.js Git Branch URL Variable

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/environment-variables/framework-environment-variables

The domain name of the generated Git branch URL. Available at build and runtime.

```bash
REDACTED.vercel.app
```

--------------------------------

### Disable deployments for specific branches in Vercel

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/project-configuration/git-configuration

Use the deploymentEnabled object to map specific branch names to boolean values. Unspecified branches default to true.

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://openapi.vercel.sh/vercel.json",
  "git": {
    "deploymentEnabled": {
      "dev": false
    }
  }
}
```

```typescript
import type { VercelConfig } from '@vercel/config/v1';

export const config: VercelConfig = {
  git: {
    deploymentEnabled: {
      dev: false,
    },
  },
};
```

--------------------------------

### Override Ignore Build Step Command in vercel.ts

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/project-configuration/vercel-ts

Use `ignoreCommand` to specify a custom command for determining if a build should be ignored. The build continues if the command exits with code 1, and is ignored if it exits with 0.

```typescript
import type { VercelConfig } from '@vercel/config/v1';

export const config: VercelConfig = {
  ignoreCommand: 'git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD ./',
};
```

